	return err;
```
Reason: Instead of returning directly, the error paths now set an error code and jump to a common `free_sync` label. The cleanup function `xe_sync_entry_cleanup` releases all previously allocated references (syncobj, fence, chain fences) and resets the sync entry. This ensures no resources leak and leaves the sync entry in a consistent state before returning the error.

